<p>Are all happy classrooms alike? Probably not. But perhaps there&#8217;s some qualities common to many of them.<span id="more-56680"></span></p>
<p>In the following guest post, <a href="https://www.danielstory.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Daniel Story</a>, assistant professor of philosophy at California Polytechnic State University, suggests that among those qualities are care and connection.</p>
<p>His experiences teaching this semester push against the dominant pessimistic narrative about today&#8217;s college students and their ability and willingness to read, to think, to do the work.</p>
<p>Read on, and perhaps you&#8217;ll be inspired to take a different approach to your teaching.</p>
